-- title:
--   The martingale-problem past contains the present observation
-- statement:
--   For any E-valued process X, the sigma-algebra generated by the present observation X_s is contained in the past sigma-algebra processPast X s, defined as the supremum over all observation times r <= s. This is the measurability inclusion behind the Markov-property conjunct of the martingale characterization: conditioning on the past refines conditioning on the present, so the representation of the conditional expectation as a function of X_s is well posed.
-- source:
--   Isolates the elementary filtration inclusion used in the Ethier-Kurtz martingale-problem characterization (parent b1aead5f): s belongs to Set.Iic s, so comap (X s) is one term of the defining supremum. Provable by le_iSup with no probability theory; the parent uses it to relate conditioning on processPast X s to conditioning on X s.

